'''Indian Baliscans''' ({{Lang-bl|Indios}} or ''Indo-baliscanos'') are people with ancestry from [[W:India|India]] who are citizens of the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. With a population of more than 5 million in the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]], Indian Baliscans make up approximately 3.24% of the Baliscan population and are the largest group of [[South Asian Baliscans]] and the second-largest group of [[Asian Baliscans]] (after [[Chinese Baliscans]]). 

